1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,404
On your phone, in a friend's status —
someone has settled in Canada.

2
00:00:05,444 --> 00:00:09,286
They post status after status from Canada.

3
00:00:09,326 --> 00:00:12,849
Photo after photo.

4
00:00:12,889 --> 00:00:17,472
Relatives ask: "Get our boy there somehow
too."

5
00:00:17,512 --> 00:00:21,034
For 90s middle-class parents, a child
settled abroad brings security and pride.

6
00:00:21,074 --> 00:00:25,757
Unmatched pride and security.

7
00:00:25,797 --> 00:00:28,699
Respect for the parents rises overnight at
every function.

8
00:00:28,739 --> 00:00:35,123
But behind this Canada settlement there is
a dark side.

9
00:00:35,163 --> 00:00:39,666
In Surrey, British Columbia...

10
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:44,169
...a 26-year-old from Khammam works behind
a small phone-shop counter.

11
00:00:44,209 --> 00:00:47,892
Came on a study visa, enrolled in college
— never attended a single class.

12
00:00:47,932 --> 00:00:54,917
Full-time in that shop, paid cash — just 7
Canadian dollars an hour.

13
00:00:54,957 --> 00:01:00,220
In Toronto, a 25-year-old from Ongole
works as a delivery agent.

14
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:04,123
Both are real stories reported by The
Times of India.

15
00:01:04,163 --> 00:01:10,347
Can we say there is no such struggle
behind every "Settled bro" photo?

16
00:01:10,387 --> 00:01:12,188
Can we really say there is no struggle?

17
00:01:12,228 --> 00:01:17,732
On 5 November 2026 the Government of
Canada made a big announcement.

18
00:01:17,772 --> 00:01:22,215
After two years of cutting immigration and
tightening visa rules...

19
00:01:22,255 --> 00:01:26,718
...the government that seemed to shut its
doors on Indian students...

20
00:01:26,758 --> 00:01:34,723
...now offers about 200,000 temporary
residents already in Canada a chance at PR
by the end of 2027.

21
00:01:34,763 --> 00:01:40,147
On top of the regular quota.

22
00:01:40,187 --> 00:01:55,897
The twist: Indians getting PR fell by
~15,000 in Jan–Jul 2026; two of every
three seats cut were Indian.

23
00:01:55,937 --> 00:02:01,701
So is Canada opening its doors for us, or
closing them?

24
00:02:01,741 --> 00:02:08,766
How the craze began, the U-turn, why
Indians were hit, ground reality, the
200,000 PR plan.

25
00:02:08,806 --> 00:02:14,410
...and the game behind the new 200,000 PR
plan.

26
00:02:14,450 --> 00:02:23,876
Three questions at the end — not easy to
answer.

27
00:02:23,916 --> 00:02:30,861
Truth first: Canada was never Telugu
families' first choice — America was.

28
00:02:30,901 --> 00:02:34,023
Ten years ago in Hyderabad, Vijayawada,
Guntur...

29
00:02:34,063 --> 00:02:39,787
"After B.Tech, where will the boy go?" —
one answer: the US.

30
00:02:39,827 --> 00:02:46,563
But America has a headache: the H-1B
lottery.

31
00:02:46,603 --> 00:02:52,135
Masters, job offer — still pure luck.

32
00:02:52,175 --> 00:02:56,618
Even with H-1B, Indians wait decades for a
green card.

33
00:02:56,658 --> 00:03:00,160
Right in that frustration, another
country's name reached our ears...

34
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:05,644
...a peaceful country with no lottery:
Canada.

35
00:03:05,684 --> 00:03:21,374
The offer was a formula: study 1–2 years,
get a PGWP, work a year, collect points,
get PR, then citizenship.

36
00:03:21,414 --> 00:03:24,455
No lottery, no luck — just a formula.

37
00:03:24,495 --> 00:03:28,619
We grew up memorising formulas; we loved
this one.

38
00:03:28,659 --> 00:03:32,079
In 2022 India was No.

39
00:03:32,119 --> 00:03:40,647
1 among new international students — over
2.26 lakh.

40
00:03:40,687 --> 00:03:48,512
In 2023, about 1.4 lakh Indians got PR —
highest in ten years.

41
00:03:48,552 --> 00:03:54,096
Roughly one of every four new PRs was
Indian.

42
00:03:54,136 --> 00:04:01,221
In Ameerpet, a consultancy board lit up on
every floor.

43
00:04:01,261 --> 00:04:03,662
Families sold farmland back home...

44
00:04:03,702 --> 00:04:08,285
...and took loans of ₹20, 30, even 40
lakh.

45
00:04:08,325 --> 00:04:16,531
Sell land, borrow ₹40 lakh, send the son
for a one-year diploma...

46
00:04:16,571 --> 00:04:20,454
...and everyone called it a wise decision
— because back then, it really worked.

47
00:04:20,494 --> 00:04:30,340
The country that wrote the formula tore it
up and threw it in the bin.

48
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:38,305
Until 2024, Ottawa's target was 5 lakh PRs
a year.

49
00:04:38,345 --> 00:05:04,023
Within two years the plan was scrapped:
483,640 (2024) → ~393,500 (2025) → 380,000
target, frozen to 2029.

50
00:05:04,063 --> 00:05:16,571
Priority now: healthcare workers,
tradespeople, French speakers, Canadian
work experience.

51
00:05:16,611 --> 00:05:22,275
Provinces got more power — nominations
raised to 95,000 a year.

52
00:05:22,315 --> 00:05:29,740
Canada no longer wants everyone — only
certain places, jobs and people.

53
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:38,185
Age 24, a generic one-year business
diploma, no French — not good news.

54
00:05:38,225 --> 00:05:44,049
Why did a country that kept saying "come,
come" suddenly pull the handbrake?

55
00:05:44,089 --> 00:05:45,063
Four reasons.

56
00:05:45,103 --> 00:05:51,955
The fourth is uncomfortable to hear.

57
00:05:51,995 --> 00:05:53,772
Reason one: housing.

58
00:05:53,812 --> 00:05:57,859
Population grew faster than homes were
built.

59
00:05:57,899 --> 00:06:07,045
In the GTA the average house price crossed
C$1 million — about 9× family income.

60
00:06:07,085 --> 00:06:14,510
Government says growth must slow so
housing and hospitals can catch up.

61
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:22,935
But a government study: immigration
explains only ~11% of 2006–2021 price
rises.

62
00:06:22,975 --> 00:06:35,163
The rest: interest rates, zoning,
investors, decades of under-building.

63
00:06:35,203 --> 00:06:39,786
Immigrants are just the most visible face
— not the main cause.

64
00:06:39,826 --> 00:06:43,022
Reason two: public mood.

65
00:06:43,062 --> 00:06:50,033
Late 2024, 54% said too many immigrants
were coming.

66
00:06:50,073 --> 00:06:55,477
When over half think so, every party has
to listen.

67
00:06:55,517 --> 00:06:57,959
Reason three: jobs — especially for youth.

68
00:06:57,999 --> 00:07:03,402
Youth unemployment hit 14.3% in April
2026.

69
00:07:03,442 --> 00:07:13,089
A Fraser Institute study argues newcomers
competed with local youth in restaurants,
retail, gas stations.

70
00:07:13,129 --> 00:07:17,071
Entry-level jobs: restaurants, retail, gas
stations.

71
00:07:17,111 --> 00:07:23,776
Other analysts: the link isn't proven;
weak hiring and trade uncertainty matter
too.

72
00:07:23,816 --> 00:07:29,099
Reason four: fraud — fake admission
letters, paper-only colleges, students who
never attend.

73
00:07:29,139 --> 00:07:34,543
Canada cracked down on all of it.

74
00:07:34,583 --> 00:07:49,973
Aug 2025: ~74% of Indian study-permit
applications refused — vs 32% two years
earlier; overall ~40%.

75
00:07:50,013 --> 00:07:54,476
What many forget: Canada built this
system.

76
00:07:54,516 --> 00:07:59,880
Colleges earned on international fees;
governments set big targets and approved
permits.

77
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:04,763
When the system overheated, the bill fell
on the least powerful — students.

78
00:08:04,803 --> 00:08:18,072
Is this correcting mistakes, or
sacrificing others?

79
00:08:18,112 --> 00:08:36,624
Jan–Jul 2025: 68,690 Indians got PR;
Jan–Jul 2026: 53,285.

80
00:08:36,664 --> 00:08:46,151
Total PR intake fell ~24,000 — 64% of the
seats cut were Indian.

81
00:08:46,191 --> 00:08:59,760
Students fared worse: new study permits
down 66% vs 2023.

82
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:03,027
So is Canada deliberately targeting
Indians?

83
00:09:03,067 --> 00:09:04,363
Set emotion aside.

84
00:09:04,403 --> 00:09:09,906
There is not a single rule written against
Indians in the official data.

85
00:09:09,946 --> 00:09:17,150
Simple and harsh: Indians are the biggest
group in the pipeline.

86
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:23,035
Narrow the pipe and the biggest flow is
hit hardest.

87
00:09:23,075 --> 00:09:28,339
In parallel, a diplomatic layer.

88
00:09:28,379 --> 00:09:33,342
Sept 2023: Trudeau alleged Indian agents
were behind Nijjar's killing.

89
00:09:33,382 --> 00:09:44,770
India rejected it, calling Nijjar a
terrorist; diplomats expelled, visa
services halted, relations frozen.

90
00:09:44,810 --> 00:09:49,113
After Mark Carney became PM, things
changed.

91
00:09:49,153 --> 00:09:53,756
Modi invited to the June 2025 G7; High
Commissioners returned.

92
00:09:53,796 --> 00:10:00,480
March 2026: Carney in Delhi, a "fresh
start" with a $50B trade target by 2030.

93
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:06,463
Diplomats shook hands, but immigration
numbers did not rise.

94
00:10:06,503 --> 00:10:10,487
These cuts come from internal pressure,
not diplomacy.

95
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:18,953
And that pressure shows on the permits of
lakhs already there.

96
00:10:18,993 --> 00:10:24,215
Now, those already there — their time is
running out.

97
00:10:24,255 --> 00:10:30,140
Their time is running out.

98
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:45,991
Permits issued in a boom now expire
together: ~1.05M expired by end-2025;
~927,000 more in 2026.

99
00:10:46,031 --> 00:10:51,754
Over 3.1 lakh in Q1 2026 alone — a record.

100
00:10:51,794 --> 00:11:03,782
Without PR or another visa: leave, apply
and wait, or stay without legal status.

101
00:11:03,822 --> 00:11:10,167
One immigration consultant estimates about
half of those affected are Indians.

102
00:11:10,207 --> 00:11:27,778
For the first time in decades, the
temporary-resident count is falling: 3.15M
→ 2.56M.

103
00:11:27,818 --> 00:11:34,603
30% of the drop moved to PR; many of the
rest packed their bags and left.

104
00:11:34,643 --> 00:11:37,473
How many stayed on without status?

105
00:11:37,513 --> 00:11:39,246
Canada has no answer.

106
00:11:39,286 --> 00:11:42,018
So what is daily life like?

107
00:11:42,058 --> 00:11:47,131
The story behind the photo.

108
00:11:47,171 --> 00:11:49,064
In the photo: snow, coffee cup, CN Tower.

109
00:11:49,104 --> 00:11:49,913
Outside the photo?

110
00:11:49,953 --> 00:11:53,741
Struggle one: jobs.

111
00:11:53,781 --> 00:12:01,801
Oct 2026 unemployment 6.7%; youth 13.7%.

112
00:12:01,841 --> 00:12:10,267
April: student unemployment 16% — one in
six job-seeking students can't find work.

113
00:12:10,307 --> 00:12:15,230
They compete for part-time jobs at coffee
chains, big-box stores, gas stations.

114
00:12:15,270 --> 00:12:17,091
Against other international students — and
our own people.

115
00:12:17,131 --> 00:12:25,077
Recent immigrants depend on gig apps five
times more: 8% vs 1.5%.

116
00:12:25,117 --> 00:12:30,300
Struggle two: rent.

117
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:36,744
Sept 2026: Toronto one-bedroom median
C$2,150/month — about ₹1.3 lakh.

118
00:12:36,784 --> 00:12:41,207
68% of monthly expenses go to rent.

119
00:12:41,247 --> 00:12:45,530
Rents are easing a little, but still high.

120
00:12:45,570 --> 00:12:50,514
Even 30% of local Canadians struggle with
basics.

121
00:12:50,554 --> 00:12:55,277
Third: our Telugu story — a community
leaders' meeting in Toronto.

122
00:12:55,317 --> 00:13:09,046
80% of Telugu graduates once got permits
and jobs; now 20% — a community estimate.

123
00:13:09,086 --> 00:13:13,229
Think of a Warangal or Nellore family that
sold land for this degree.

124
00:13:13,269 --> 00:13:14,341
Degree done.

125
00:13:14,381 --> 00:13:16,101
Loan still running.

126
00:13:16,141 --> 00:13:16,750
No job.

127
00:13:16,790 --> 00:13:18,232
Permit expiring.

128
00:13:18,272 --> 00:13:22,795
Yet the photo sent home shows snow, a
coffee cup, a smile.

129
00:13:22,835 --> 00:13:31,721
In all this hardship, is society
supportive — or is something else
happening?

130
00:13:31,761 --> 00:13:35,763
When the economy is hard, people look for
someone to blame.

131
00:13:35,803 --> 00:13:38,566
In Canada that blame fell on Indians.

132
00:13:38,606 --> 00:13:48,672
One analysis: posts with anti-South Asian
slurs on X rose 1,350%+ from 2023 to 2024.

133
00:13:48,712 --> 00:13:52,375
A false viral video claimed Indians were
misusing Wasaga Beach.

134
00:13:52,415 --> 00:13:55,877
Fake video, gone viral.

135
00:13:55,917 --> 00:14:02,922
Anonymous accounts posted AI images of
Indian flags over Canadian cities: "Canada
in 2050".

136
00:14:02,962 --> 00:14:12,588
Newcomers say they brace themselves before
opening the comments.

137
00:14:12,628 --> 00:14:17,792
Not new: in 1914 the Komagata Maru was
turned back under racial laws.

138
00:14:17,832 --> 00:14:22,515
Turned back under racially exclusionary
laws.

139
00:14:22,555 --> 00:14:29,660
A century on, the words changed but the
fear stayed.

140
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:34,943
Most ordinary Canadians have no hatred —
they are exhausted.

141
00:14:34,983 --> 00:14:38,766
Can't pay rent, kids can't find jobs,
hours waiting in hospitals.

142
00:14:38,806 --> 00:14:41,706
Anger at a system that grew too fast.

143
00:14:41,746 --> 00:14:44,169
Anger is different from hatred.

144
00:14:44,209 --> 00:14:48,532
But that anger lands on the most visible
Indian face.

145
00:14:48,572 --> 00:14:58,899
Irony: some Indians settled years ago now
say "cut immigration" — closing the door
opened for them.

146
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:06,824
Amid all this anger and cuts, why open a
back door?

147
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:11,908
Back to the 5 November 2026 announcement.

148
00:15:11,948 --> 00:15:18,272
Budget 2026 holds regular limits to 2029:
380,000 PR, 370,000 temporary arrivals.

149
00:15:18,312 --> 00:15:33,702
On top: a one-time measure for 200,000
already in Canada by end-2027 — 100,000
workers, 100,000 humanitarian/family.

150
00:15:33,742 --> 00:15:40,787
Before this, another one-time program for
33,000 workers.

151
00:15:40,827 --> 00:15:45,390
Why would a government that cut for two
years suddenly open this door?

152
00:15:45,430 --> 00:15:47,231
A problem of its own making.

153
00:15:47,271 --> 00:15:51,174
Lakhs already work inside the country,
paying taxes and rent.

154
00:15:51,214 --> 00:15:55,797
Deporting them is expensive and a
political headache.

155
00:15:55,837 --> 00:15:59,419
Left without status, an underground
economy forms.

156
00:15:59,459 --> 00:16:03,832
Converting the ones it needs to PR is the
cheapest way.

157
00:16:03,872 --> 00:16:08,726
Canada isn't inviting newcomers — it's
choosing whom to keep.

158
00:16:08,766 --> 00:16:10,831
Not automatic PR.

159
00:16:10,871 --> 00:16:13,680
Not everyone qualifies.

160
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:17,271
Full rules not yet published.

161
00:16:17,311 --> 00:16:23,936
An expert said even the earlier 33,000
program raised false hopes.

162
00:16:23,976 --> 00:16:30,960
PM Carney defends it; opposition leader
Pierre Poilievre calls it a "disaster".

163
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:37,945
The only question for our kids: "Am I in
the group Canada wants to keep?"

164
00:16:37,985 --> 00:16:44,627
Back to that WhatsApp group: the "Settled
bro" photo, 40 replies.

165
00:16:44,667 --> 00:16:46,991
Has your angle changed?

166
00:16:47,031 --> 00:17:02,241
Five realities no consultancy will tell
you.

167
00:17:02,281 --> 00:17:14,349
Only healthcare, trades, French, in-demand
Canadian experience give PR chances.

168
00:17:14,389 --> 00:17:26,838
If an agent says part-time work will pay
the fees — walk out.

169
00:17:26,878 --> 00:17:33,942
Smaller provinces and rural areas have
clearer paths than Toronto or Vancouver.

170
00:17:33,982 --> 00:17:45,390
Budget: show at least ~C$20,600 for living
costs besides tuition; rent eats most
income in big cities.

171
00:17:45,430 --> 00:17:58,839
Alternatives: many Telugu students now
look at Germany and New Zealand.

172
00:17:58,879 --> 00:18:02,039
Opening or closing?

173
00:18:02,079 --> 00:18:12,649
Neither — Canada opens its door for
itself, for those it needs.

174
00:18:12,689 --> 00:18:16,491
Not a villain, not a paradise — a country
dealing with its own problems.

175
00:18:16,531 --> 00:18:20,473
That Khammam boy did nothing unusual — he
followed the formula everyone followed.

176
00:18:20,513 --> 00:18:29,760
Consultancies sold it, relatives believed
it; Canada rewarded it for a few years,
then changed its mind.

177
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:31,881
Dreaming of going abroad isn't wrong...

178
00:18:31,921 --> 00:18:40,667
...betting the family's land on a policy
that changes with one budget is.

179
00:18:40,707 --> 00:19:12,068
So I leave you three questions.

180
00:19:12,108 --> 00:19:16,150
Comment your answers; share this video
with friends or family planning to go
abroad.

181
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:24,440
Until Canada publishes the rules for the
200,000 PR plan — thanks for watching.

